STEP 7: securityContext hardening
---------------------------------
kubectx kind-calico   (any cluster works for this part)
k create ns secure

vi pod-root.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: root-pod
  namespace: secure
spec:
  containers:
  - name: c
    image: busybox:1.36
    command: ["sleep", "3600"]

k apply -f pod-root.yaml
k exec -n secure root-pod -- id                 # uid=0(root)
k exec -n secure root-pod -- touch /etc/hacked && echo "wrote to /etc"

vi pod-hardened.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: hardened
  namespace: secure
spec:
  securityContext:
    runAsNonRoot: true
    runAsUser: 10001
    runAsGroup: 10001
    seccompProfile:
      type: RuntimeDefault
  containers:
  - name: c
    image: busybox:1.36
    command: ["sleep", "3600"]
    securityContext:
      allowPrivilegeEscalation: false
      readOnlyRootFilesystem: true
      capabilities:
        drop: ["ALL"]
    volumeMounts:
    - name: tmp
      mountPath: /tmp
  volumes:
  - name: tmp
    emptyDir: {}

k apply -f pod-hardened.yaml
k exec -n secure hardened -- id                     # uid=10001
k exec -n secure hardened -- touch /etc/hacked      # Read-only file system
k exec -n secure hardened -- touch /tmp/ok && echo "tmp writable"


STEP 8: Pod Security Admission
------------------------------
k label ns secure pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce=restricted --overwrite
(existing pods are not removed; warnings are shown)

k delete pod root-pod -n secure
k apply -f pod-root.yaml          # REJECTED: lists every violation
k apply -f pod-hardened.yaml      # allowed (already exists = unchanged)

Try "baseline" with a privileged pod:
  k label ns secure pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce=baseline --overwrite
  k run priv -n secure --image=busybox:1.36 --overrides='{"spec":{"containers":[{"name":"priv","image":"busybox:1.36","command":["sleep","3600"],"securityContext":{"privileged":true}}]}}'
  -> rejected

Warn mode on another namespace:
  k label ns other pod-security.kubernetes.io/warn=restricted
  k run w -n other --image=nginx:1.27      # created, but with warnings


